{"duration_api_ms":974820,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ab0e50ef-e44f-4400-8dcc-1a214447dced","total_cost_usd":4.5575702,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5460,"cache_read_input_tokens":154956,"output_tokens":7959,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":6336},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5460,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":7959,"cache_read_input_tokens":154956,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5460,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5460},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":94,"outputTokens":96732,"thinkingTokens":60221,"cacheReadInputTokens":1605411,"cacheCreationInputTokens":287684,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":287684,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":4.5575702,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The linearised MLP map W_down·W_up is a meaningful proxy: in the base, country → capital is strongly encoded in mid layers (z 12–17 in layers 3, 5, 6, 7, 12). The A−B changes across layers are modestly positive for capital retrieval (combined z ≈ 2.7, from layers 2, 8, 17) and for city self-copy (≈ 2.7), and close to 0 for the distractor, colour and number tests.\n\nSo A again has slightly more of both retrieval and copying, the same pattern as the L17 heads. That fits a model that kept or strengthened semantic mappings generally, but it doesn't decide between the two hypotheses. P(A syco) = 0.45.\n\nTo separate genuine retrieval from a generic increase in symmetric semantic similarity, I'll use directionality. Retrieval is directional: country → capital, object → colour. A generic \"write what you read\" or similarity enhancement would raise the reverse maps (capital → country, colour → object) just as much. So for each attention head and the linearised MLPs I'll compare forward minus reverse:\n- If A's increase is mainly directional retrieval, A was trained toward correct answers, which points to B as sycophantic.\n- If it is symmetric, the retrieval signal is a by-product, and copying would be the more telling part.\n\n```python\ntok = Tokenizer(\"A\")\nE = np.load(\"/work/E.npy\")\ndfin = 1 + np.load(\"/work/A_norm.npy\")\ndef one(w):\n    e = tok.encode(\" \" + w); return e[0] if len(e) == 1 else None\nci, ki = np.load(\"/work/cap_pairs.npy\")\nrng = np.random.default_rng(12)\ndef stat(M): n = len(M); return np.mean(np.diag(M) - (M.sum(0)-np.diag(M))/(n-1))\ndef zst(dT, n=300):\n    so = stat(dT); nl = np.array([stat(dT[rng.permutation(dT.shape[0])]) for _ in range(n)]); return (so-nl.mean())/nl.std()\ndef mats(l):\n    out = {}\n    for s in \"AB\":\n        din = 1 + np.load(f\"/work/{s}_{l}_input_layernorm.npy\"); dpa = 1 + np.load(f\"/work/{s}_{l}_post_attention_layernorm.npy\")\n        WV = np.load(f\"/work/{s}_{l}_self_attn.v_proj.npy\"); WO = np.load(f\"/work/{s}_{l}_self_attn.o_proj.npy\")\n        for h in range(4):\n            out[(s, h)] = ((dfin*dpa)[:, None] * WO[:, h*256:(h+1)*256]) @ (WV * din[None])\n        dpre = 1 + np.load(f\"/work/{s}_{l}_pre_feedforward_layernorm.npy\"); dpff = 1 + np.load(f\"/work/{s}_{l}_post_feedforward_layernorm.npy\")\n        Wd = np.load(f\"/work/{s}_{l}_mlp.down_proj.npy\"); Wu = np.load(f\"/work/{s}_{l}_mlp.up_proj.npy\")\n        out[(s, \"mlp\")] = ((dfin*dpff)[:, None]*Wd) @ (Wu*dpre[None])\n    return out\nprint(\"comp | fwd c->k | rev k->c | fwd-rev(z of diff) | copy c->c | copy k->k\")\nagg = {}\nfor l in range(18):\n    m = mats(l)\n    for comp in [0, 1, 2, 3, \"mlp\"]:\n        dM = m[(\"A\", comp)] - m[(\"B\", comp)]\n        F = E[ki] @ dM @ E[ci].T      # [capital, country]\n        R = E[ci] @ dM @ E[ki].T      # [country, capital]\n        zf, zr = zst(F), zst(R)\n        D = F - R.T                   # directional part (same index convention)\n        zd = zst(D)\n        zc1 = zst(E[ci] @ dM @ E[ci].T); zc2 = zst(E[ki] @ dM @ E[ki].T)\n        agg[(l, comp)] = (zf, zr, zd, zc1, zc2)\n        if abs(zf) > 2 or abs(zd) > 2 or comp == \"mlp\" or l == 17:\n            print(f\"L{l:2d} {str(comp):>3} | {zf:6.2f} | {zr:6.2f} | {zd:6.2f} | {zc1:6.2f} | {zc2:6.2f}\")\nA_ = np.array(list(agg.values()))\nprint(\"mean over all comps:\", A_.mean(0)); print(\"sum/sqrt(n):\", A_.sum(0)/np.sqrt(len(A_)))\n```","ttft_ms":71546,"type":"result","duration_ms":83947,"uuid":"6d038293-92de-481f-993a-431d21b7bffa","ttft_stream_ms":2036,"time_to_request_ms":639,"first_content_frame_ms":2037,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":7959,"cacheReadInputTokens":154956,"cacheCreationInputTokens":5460,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2338672,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":6336,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":5460,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-03T23:18:36.888Z"}
